        "PMC9960858::web::021::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pre-oxidation at 700–750 °C and an oxygen partial pressure of 10^-3–10^-2 atm will produce the intended oxide layer.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The pre-formed oxide layer will be adherent and coherent.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "An oxide tribolayer can act as a protective solid lubricant.",
